    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, as long as either a card with [Beelzemon] or [Ai & Mako] is among the cards revealed, you can add it to your hand.",
        "question": "This card’s effect reveals 4 cards. If the cards revealed only include either a card with [Beelzemon] or [Ai & Mako], can I still add a card to my hand?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. This card's effect reads “Add 1 card [...] among them to your hand,” so you must add as many cards to your hand as possible. In this case, you must add both 1 card with [Beelzemon], and 1 [Ai & Mako] to your hand.",
        "question": "This card’s effect reveals 4 cards. If both a card with [Beelzemon] and [Ai & Mako] are among the cards revealed, can I choose to only add one of them to my hand, and place the remaining card at the bottom of my deck?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, cards revealed from the top of your deck aren't considered to be “trashed from your deck,” so this card’s effect doesn’t activate.",
        "question": "An effect that reads, “Reveal a card from your deck” reveals this card and trashes it. Does this card's “When this card is trashed from your deck” effect activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes. This effect specifies a specific card number (EX2-039 Impmon), so as long as the effect is from a card with a different card number, the effect will activate.",
        "question": "If the effect of [BT2-068 Impmon] trashes this card from my deck, does this card’s “When this card is trashed from your deck” effect activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
